{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1559","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Mocha and Stars"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mocha wants to be an astrologer. There are $$$n$$$ stars which can be seen in Zhijiang, and the brightness of the $$$i$$$-th star is $$$a_i$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mocha considers that these $$$n$$$ stars form a constellation, and she uses $$$(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n)$$$ to show its state. A state is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mathematical"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if all of the following three conditions are satisfied:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For all $$$i$$$ ($$$1\\le i\\le n$$$), $$$a_i$$$ is an integer in the range $$$[l_i, r_i]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\sum \\limits _{i=1} ^ n a_i \\le m$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\gcd(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n)=1$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here, $$$\\gcd(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor (GCD)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mocha is wondering how many different mathematical states of this constellation exist. Because the answer may be large, you must find it modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two states $$$(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n)$$$ and $$$(b_1,b_2,\\ldots,b_n)$$$ are considered different if there exists $$$i$$$ ($$$1\\le i\\le n$$$) such that $$$a_i \\ne b_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 50$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of stars and the upper bound of the sum of the brightness of stars."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains two integers $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le l_i \\le r_i \\le m$$$) — the range of the brightness of the $$$i$$$-th star."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the number of different mathematical states of this constellation, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 4\n1 3\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 10\n1 10\n1 10\n1 10\n1 10\n1 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n251"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 100\n1 94\n1 96\n1 91\n4 96\n6 97\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n47464146"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are $$$4$$$ different mathematical states of this constellation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1=1$$$, $$$a_2=1$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1=1$$$, $$$a_2=2$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1=2$$$, $$$a_2=1$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1=3$$$, $$$a_2=1$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1559E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1559/problem/E"}